==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{wikispecies}}
[[Image:Tree dsc00854.jpg|thumb]]

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|Magnol|lang1=fr|ia}}. Named after French botanist {{w|Pierre Magnol}} (1638–1715). The surname is a form of the male given name ''Magne,'' from {{der|en|la|magnus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˌmæɡˈnoʊ.li.ə/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-magnolia.wav|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[tree]] or [[shrub]] in any species of the [[genus]] ''[[Magnolia]]'', many with large flowers and [[simple]] [[leaf|leaves]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=w:Jesmyn Ward|title=w:Salvage the Bones|publisher=Bloomsbury (2017)|page=158|passage=There are clusters of '''magnolias''' that are so tall and green and glossy, they are impossible to climb, and the air around them always smells like peaches.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} The [[flower]] of a magnolia tree.
# {{lb|en|countable}} A native or resident of the American state of [[Mississippi]].
# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable}} A creamy [[white]] colour, like that of some magnolia flowers.
#: {{color panel|F8EDD3}}

